REFERENCE   2  (bases 1 to 1830)
  AUTHORS   Fan,P., Han,B., Feng,M., Fang,Y., Zhang,L., Hu,H., Hao,Y., Qi,Y.,
            Zhang,X. and Li,J.
  TITLE     Functional and Proteomic Investigations Reveal Major Royal Jelly
            Protein 1 Associated with Anti-hypertension Activity in Mouse
            Vascular Smooth Muscle Cells
  JOURNAL   Sci Rep 6, 30230 (2016)
   PUBMED   27444336
  REMARK    GeneRIF: Among 675 different proteins after MRJP1 expression, 646
            were down-regulated and significantly enriched in pathways
            implicated in VSMC contraction and migration, which suggest MRJP1
            lowers VSMC contraction and migration by inhibiting muscle filament
            movement. This is the first report integrating MRJP1 into VSMC,
            revealing the function and mechanism correlated with
            anti-hypertensive activity.
            Publication Status: Online-Only
